regression.why:
Requirement 2, at the one call that decides whether anything else happens. The vendored helper is

    func FileExists(filePath string) bool {
        if _, err := os.Stat(filePath); !os.IsNotExist(err) {
            return true
        }
        return false
    }

-- an absolute path, statted outside any root, reported as present for every error that is not `does not exist`. It is the only guard on the driver's four lookup paths and it constrains nothing about where the path points. Eighteen calls in the tree; four of them are in `drivers/storage/vfs/storage` and those four are the ones a confined lookup replaces.

A floor of fourteen rather than of zero because the other fourteen are not this step's: five in the vfs executor, which manages a device file and not the data directory, and nine spread across configuration, TLS material and the CLI. Graded, so each of the four is worth a quarter, and a tree that cleans up the other fourteen as well reads below the floor and is clamped at full marks rather than rewarded for scope it was not asked for.

Worth 3 of 38. This is the call that makes the trap in requirement 5 possible -- a name the filesystem itself rejects is reported by it as present, and reaches the open -- so replacing it is the place where the message a caller reads is most easily lost.
